    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d510-a3">

                <pb facs="0841" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg705"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 809.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sewall to Mr.
                            Rives.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Apia, Samoa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 28, 1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 84.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    copies of proclamation signed by Tamasese and Brandeis, announcing that in
                    consequence of the withdrawal of the Imperial German Government from the
                    convention of September 2, 1879, the former municipal district passes under the
                    control of this Government, and declaring which of the former municipal
                    regulations are still in force. Foreigners are left under foreign
                    jurisdiction.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harold Marsh
                                Sewall</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
